          Executive Summary: The Cheapest Auto Insurers in 2026
        </div>
        <ul class="callout-list">
          <li><strong>Cheapest Overall:</strong> <strong>USAA ($1,480/yr)</strong> provides the lowest national average rates for military members and qualifying family. Among non-military carriers, <strong>GEICO ($1,865/yr)</strong> and <strong>State Farm ($1,940/yr)</strong> offer the most competitive national pricing.</li>
          <li><strong>Cheapest Regional Standouts:</strong> In states where they operate, regional mutual carriers like <strong>Erie Insurance ($1,438/yr)</strong> and <strong>Auto-Owners ($1,620/yr)</strong> consistently beat national television advertisers by 20% to 25%.</li>
          <li><strong>The Credit Score Factor:</strong> For drivers with poor credit, <strong>GEICO</strong> and <strong>Nationwide</strong> impose the smallest rate surcharges compared to peers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <p class="lead-text">
        Every major auto insurer claims you can save hundreds of dollars by switching to their policy. But when rate filings from all 50 state insurance departments are aggregated and evaluated under identical testing profiles, which carriers actually deliver the lowest true premiums?
      </p>

      <h2>The 6 Cheapest Car Insurance Companies of 2026</h2>
      <p>
        The table below benchmarks average annual premiums for full coverage (100/300/100 liability limits, $500 collision/comprehensive deductibles) across four distinct risk profiles:
      </p>

